## Part D — Webcam placement (so counts are clean)

* The pink line is the doorway. The grey dashed lines either side are the **arm zone**. A person
  counts only when they go from beyond one dashed line to beyond the other. Standing or sitting
  near the line never counts.
* Point the camera **across** the doorway so people walk sideways through the frame, from left
  (outside) to right (inside). If your door runs the other way, press `r` (reverse) or `o` (horizontal line).
* Don't test by sitting in front of the laptop with the line through your body. Stand up and walk across.
* Track numbers (1, 21, 34…) are just tracker IDs, not people's identities. See the main README.

## Demo-day checklist
1. Hotspot on (2.4 GHz) → laptop connected → `ipconfig` shows the firmware's IP.
2. Backend → vision → ngrok running.
3. Phone check: `http://<laptop-IP>:8000/health` works.
4. Dashboard on Streamlit Cloud shows **LIVE LINK** and **SENTRY ONLINE**.
5. Tap a card, then walk one person across: **Authorised entry**. Walk two people across: **Tailgating**, with a PDF in the feed.
